THIRD-PARTY ATTRIBUTION
=======================

src/cleft/models/srgnn.py
-------------------------

This file is a port of the SR-GNN reference implementation released at:

    https://github.com/ArdhenduBehera/SR-GNN

for the paper:

    Bera, Wharton, Liu, Bessis & Behera, "SR-GNN: Spatial Relation-Aware
    Graph Neural Network for Fine-Grained Image Categorization", IEEE
    Transactions on Image Processing 31:6017-6031 (2022).
    https://doi.org/10.1109/TIP.2022.3205215

The port was verified by weight transplant against the released
weights: 257 of 257 weight tensors map onto the port's parameters, and
outputs match to better than 1e-6 at every internal stage, corroborated
across three checkpoints.

**That upstream repository carries no LICENSE file.** No licence was
granted publicly, so nothing was inherited from it. This file is
published here on the basis of PERMISSION GIVEN DIRECTLY, held from two
sources: the supervisor of this work, who is an author on the paper, and
the owner of the upstream repository, who is its corresponding author.
The dated record of that authorisation is at
``cleft.models.srgnn.PUBLICATION_AUTHORISED``.

**That permission covers this repository's publication of this file and
grants nothing onward.** A recipient of this repository does not thereby
receive any right to the upstream work, and the Apache-2.0 grant over
the rest of this repository does not extend to it. Anyone wishing to
reuse the SR-GNN implementation should approach the upstream authors.


src/cleft/models/agnet.py
-------------------------

NOT a port, and the distinction is deliberate. This file is a
paper-faithful implementation written from:

    Bera, Wharton, Liu, Bessis & Behera, "Attend and Guide (AG-Net): A
    Keypoints-Driven Attention-Based Deep Network for Image
    Recognition", IEEE Transactions on Image Processing 30:3691-3704
    (2021).

No authors' weights were released for AG-Net, so no weight transplant
was possible and none is claimed. The one third-party reproduction that
exists was examined and discredited, and was not used.


